    "message_excerpt": "Keep the main research line in **TRM-infusion**. Do not go all-in on MeTTa yet.\n\nThe reason is straightforward: the measurable benchmark evidence from **April 16, 2026 through April 22, 2026** is on the TRM side, while the MeTTa work is currently a promising symbolic packaging/compiler layer, not yet a demonstrated benchmark-improving intervention. The local MeTTa study says exactly that: it successfully compiled one structured-map bundle, and the next phase is wiring it into a live Hermes path, not claiming lift yet. See [metta-trm-hermes-pipeline/README.md](</C:/projects/Hermes-Skills/Hermes Skills/metta-trm-hermes-pipeline/README.md>) and [research/studies/2026-04-22-metta-trm-hermes-pipeline/experiment_log.md](</C:/projects/Hermes-Skills/Hermes Skills/research/studies/2026-04-22-metta-trm-hermes-pipeline/experiment_log.md>).\n\n**What We Learned**\n- **April 16:** the finished BlueBeam benchmark handoff was real and clean: `90/90` tasks completed, `20` new positive replays, with `14` positives from `qwen35_9b` and `6` from `qwen35_27b`. The TRM read at that point was already \u201ccritic/control-plane stronger than action imitation.\u201d Source: [data/handoffs/bluebeam_mechinterp_2026-04-16/README.md](</C:/projects/H",
